\title{Conjectural permutation decoding of some AG codes\thanks{MSC 2000: 
14H37, 94B27,20C20,11T71,14G50,05E20,14Q05}}

\maketitle

\begin{abstract}
We study the action of a finite group on the Riemann-Roch
space of certain divisors on a specific hyperelliptic curve
$X$ defined over a finite field with ``large'' automorphism group
$G$. If $D$ is a divisor on $X$ left stable by $G$ then 
the natural representation of $G$ on the Riemann-Roch space 
$L(D)=L_X(D)$. If $E=P_1+...+P_n$ is another
divisor on $X$ left stable by $G$ then this representation on
$L(D)$ induces a permutation representation on the
associated AG code $C=C(D,E)$ (defined below).
This note discusses the permutation decoding of these AG codes.

\end{abstract}
